+# Story RC4.3: Row Actions — Start, Skip, Take Over, Correct, Substitute
+
+**Status:** in-progress (briefing pre-approved — epic ACs are canonical)
+**Epic:** RC4 (Landlord Reference Panel & Workflow). Depends on RC4.2 (merged, #605).
+**Model:** `deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash` (briefing policy — execution role).
+**Perkins:** ON.
+**GitHub issue:** (none)
+
+## Story
+
+> As a landlord,
+> I want to control each check — start early, skip, take over, fix details, swap referees,
+> So that automation never traps me and a dead end always has a next step.
+
+RC4.2 rendered the panel display-only; the `⋯` overflow control ships with its testid but no
+menu (documented there as RC4.3's delivery). RC4.3 wires the landlord's control surface: the
+pre-trigger start/skip (RC2.3 APIs + the pre-declared `?slot=` per-row variant), the warm-handoff
+takeover (A7 `taken_over_at` — the sweep already skips taken-over rows; the form link stays live,
+RC3.4 already notifies on late completion), the one-cycle correction flow (AD-7/A1 landlord-driven,
+including the rc3-7-stamped second-failure terminal), and referee substitution after
+`objected`/`unreachable` (new row per slot, prior retained as history, AD-16 old+new ids).
+
+**The load-bearing rules:** (1) guarded single-UPDATE transitions on the expected pre-state
+(AD-14 — 0-row = stand down); (2) the `contact_*` snapshot is immutable — corrections land in
+`corrected_*` columns, the effective contact is `corrected ?? snapshot`; (3) every action is
+hidden entirely in the Off (declined) state (no rows exist there — server suppression + the
+panel's Off branch); (4) inline confirmations and inline edits, never a modal (§7.4/§7.7/§8.3).
+
+## Scope
+
+### OWNS
+1. **`server/src/reference_checks/actions_handler.gleam`** (NEW) — four landlord action
+   handlers following the `trigger.gleam` handler pattern (three-UUID parse, ownership +
+   archived-vacancy prechecks, branded errors, json responses):
+   - **Take over** `POST /api/v1/vacancies/:vid/applications/:aid/reference-checks/:call_id/take-over`
+     — guarded `UPDATE ... SET taken_over_at = now(), next_attempt_at = NULL WHERE id = $1 AND
+     taken_over_at IS NULL AND status IN ('queued','contact_initiated','unreachable')`
+     (waiting states + unreachable per §7.7; `unreachable` is terminal-sticky for every writer
+     BUT takeover is the one landlord-side un-stick — a deliberate, pre-declared exception: it
+     only writes `taken_over_at`/`next_attempt_at`, never status). Audit `reference_call_taken_over`.
+   - **Correct** `POST .../reference-checks/:call_id/correct` — body `{name, email, phone}`;
+     guarded `awaiting_correction → queued` with `corrected_name/email/phone = $n`
+     (empty string = NULL), `correction_cycles = correction_cycles + 1`, `next_attempt_at = now()`,
+     `terminal_reason = NULL`; ALSO updates the application trio for the slot (A1: the landlord
+     edits the slot's trio inline); audit `reference_call_corrected`. Max 1 cycle is enforced by
+     the guard: a second `correct` on a row that is no longer `awaiting_correction` 409s.
+   - **Substitute** `POST .../reference-checks/:call_id/substitute` — body `{name, email, phone}`;
+     guarded on `status IN ('objected','unreachable')` (the `can_substitute_referee` set);
+     idempotent insert of a NEW `queued` row for the same `(application_id, ref_slot,
+     owner_label)` via the existing `insert_reference_call_if_absent` (partial unique index —
+     the prior terminal row doesn't occupy the slot; a double-click conflicts → no-op, 200);
+     new row carries the new trio as its immutable snapshot; the application trio is also
+     updated; audit `reference_call_substituted` carries `old_id` + `new_id` (AD-16).
+   - **Exhaustion hook** — in `webhooks.gleam` and the wrong-person route (form_handler.gleam):
+     when the guarded failure transition finds `correction_cycles >= 1`, the row does NOT go to
+     `awaiting_correction` again — it terminalizes `→ unreachable` (guarded, `terminal_reason`
+     kept) + `stamp_referee_contact_invalid` (rc3-7 mechanism — this makes it LIVE) + audit +
+     the existing unreachable notification. The two SQL reads feeding these sites gain
+     `correction_cycles` (expand-only).
+2. **`server/src/reference_checks/trigger.gleam`** — `handle_start` gains an optional
+   `?slot=` query param (validated against the three slots; invalid → 400). Present: create
+   checks for that slot only (per-row §7.4 start). Absent: whole-application (today's
+   behaviour — expand-only). The core creation function gains an optional slot filter.
+3. **`server/src/router.gleam`** — three new POST arms (take-over / correct / substitute),
+   `require_session`-wrapped, slot-param passthrough on the start arm.
+4. **`server/src/reference_checks/sql/`** (NEW queries, squirrel):
+   `take_over_reference_call.sql`, `correct_reference_call.sql` (guard + corrected_* +
+   cycle bump + re-arm in ONE update), `substitute_reference_call.sql` (reads the old row's
+   slot/owner + verifies the pre-state guard) — plus expand-only column additions to
+   `list_reference_calls_for_detail.sql` (`taken_over_at`, `contact_name/email/phone`,
+   `corrected_name/email/phone`, `correction_cycles` — COALESCE convention), and
+   `correction_cycles` on `find_reference_call_by_send_ref.sql` +
+   `get_form_context_by_form_token.sql` (exhaustion check).
+5. **`supabase/migrations/`** (expand-only): `corrected_name TEXT` (the §8.3 edit-trio's
+   Name field; A1's corrected-* pattern extended) + `corrected_at TIMESTAMPTZ` (the
+   exhaustion gate's correction instant — r1 W3). Everything else exists since rc2-1.
+6. **`shared/src/shared/reference_call.gleam`** — additive detail keys: `taken_over_at`,
+   `contact_name`, `contact_email`, `contact_phone`, `corrected_name`, `corrected_email`,
+   `corrected_phone`, `correction_cycles` (Option/Int, back-compat `optional_field`
+   decoders) + `hooks.can_take_over`. Encoder nullable.
+7. **`server/src/application/application_detail_handler.gleam`** — map the new row fields;
+   the trio-update helper for correct/substitute lives in the actions handler (application
+   SQL: UPDATE the slot's trio columns by slot name).
+8. **`server/src/audit/event_type.gleam`** — three new variants + wire strings:
+   `reference_call_taken_over` / `reference_call_corrected` / `reference_call_substituted`.
+9. **`client/src/api/reference_checks_api.gleam`** (NEW) — `start_check(vid, aid, slot?)`,
+   `skip_reference`, `re_enable_reference`, `take_over_reference`, `correct_reference`,
+   `substitute_reference` — `api_helpers.post_json` + `csrf_token` + `api_error.map_rsvp`,
+   the `application_api.gleam` pattern.
+10. **`client/src/components/reference_panel.gleam`** — the control surface:
+    - overflow `⋯` menu (per-row open state): Queued → Start this check now / Skip this
+      reference; Skipped → Start this check (re-enable); ContactInitiated → Take over
+      manually; Unreachable → Take over manually / Substitute referee; Objected → Substitute
+      referee. AwaitingCorrection → no menu, the row detail IS the correction UI (§8.3).
+    - Start: inline one-time confirm (§7.4 verbatim confirm copy) → POST → refetch detail.
+    - Take over: inline confirm (§7.7 verbatim) → POST → row label "You're handling this one",
+      effective-contact chips render inline (from the payload's corrected??snapshot trio),
+      attempt-log export affordance renders beside them.
+    - Correct: §8.3 inline edit-trio (Name/Email/Phone, prefilled with the effective trio),
+      applicant contact chips below, "Save & resend" → POST → audit-logged server-side; error
+      states stay inline (brand copy).
+    - Substitute: same inline edit-trio (heading per §8.2) → POST → refetch; both rows render
+      (prior retained as history).
+    - The row's referee name reads from the payload `contact_name` (fall back to the app
+      trio — post-substitution rows carry their own snapshot).
+11. **`client/src/msg.gleam` + `client/src/model.gleam` + `client/src/client.gleam`** —
+    messages per action (`UserClickedRefcheckStart(Slot)`-family, `ApiReturnedRefcheckAction(Result)`
+    with a `(call_id)` match guard, menu/confirm/edit-form state, in-flight per row); refetch
+    the application detail after each successful action; reset menu/form state on route change.
+12. **`client/src/copy.gleam`** — all new strings verbatim from §7.4 (start confirm, skipped
+    state action), §7.7 (take-over confirm), §8.3 (correction copy, Save & resend), §8.2
+    (substitute), plus menu labels and the "You're handling this one" label. No inline strings.
+13. **Tests** — server unit/integration per transition: takeover guard matrix (queued/
+    contact_initiated/unreachable ok; awaiting_correction/skipped/terminals 409/404; sweep
+    exclusion + late-completion still completes — integration), correction (guarded on
+    awaiting_correction, corrected_* written + snapshot untouched, app trio updated,
+    correction_cycles = 1, re-queued next_attempt_at = now(), audit), second-failure
+    exhaustion (webhook + wrong-person: awaiting_correction→unreachable + stamp +
+    notification + audit), substitution (new row + old retained, history, audit old+new ids,
+    idempotent double-submit, guard on objected/unreachable only), per-slot start (slot param
+    creates only that slot; invalid slot 400), ownership/archived prechecks, CSRF. Client
+    tests: menu open/action wiring, inline confirms, edit-trio render/save, takeover chips +
+    label, hidden in Off, testids.
+
+### Does NOT own (deferred / sibling stories)
+- **"Ask Aisling to nudge"** — not in RC4.3's ACs (present in §7.3's overflow table but absent
+  from the story ACs and the briefing); deferred with RC4.4's notification work.
+- **Full attempt-log timeline + OQ-5 clipboard toast** — RC4.4. RC4.3 renders the export
+  affordance on the takeover surface (AC-mandated) wired to a plain clipboard copy of the
+  attempt log (no dead control; RC4.4 upgrades the text + verbatim toast + timeline).
+- **Notification completeness / preference matrix** — RC4.4.
+- **WoZ record-manual UI** — RC5.
+- **Applicant self-serve correction/substitution links** — v2 (A1).
